PR #104  overall: compliant
Spec: Without Svukte, U-mode access to S-mode memory may raise faults in address-dependent time, leaking supervisor address space layout through a timing side channel
  [OK] lib/sbi/sbi_domain_context.c:139-140  switch_to_next_domain_context
      The PR adds __sbi_sfence_vma_all() (sfence.vma) immediately after csr_swap(CSR_SATP, ...), which is exactly what the RISC-V privileged spec requires when satp is modified (mode/PPN/ASID change). Before this fix, stale TLB entries from the previous domain could remain live after the SATP switch, creating a timing oracle: an access that happens to hit a stale TLB entry resolves quickly, while one that misses incurs a page-table walk or page fault. An attacker could measure these latency differences to infer another domain's address-space layout (KASLR/ASLR bypass). The sfence.vma flushes all local-hart TLB entries, ensuring every subsequent access performs a fresh page-table walk with uniform timing characteristics, eliminating the side channel.

